# [Bug] l.fl1 instruction not decoded

- Source URL: https://github.com/openrisc/mor1kx/issues/102

@lifeasageek

l.fl1 instruction is not decoded correctly.
Any l.fl1 instruction can reproduce the error.

We can solve this with following change in mor1kx_decode.v

```verilog
  assign decode_op_ffl1_o = opc_insn == `OR1K_OPCODE_ALU &&
                        (decode_insn_i[9:8] == 2'b00 || decode_insn_i[9:8] == 2'b01) &&
                        opc_alu == `OR1K_ALU_OPC_FFL1;
```

## PR Title
Fix mor1kx_decode to accept valid l.fl1 (l.ff1) instructions

## PR Description
The pull request addresses issue #102 regarding the l.fl1 instruction decoding problem. According to the commit messages: "Both l.fl1 and l.ff1 have bit 9 set in the instruction as part of their op codes, mor1kx_decode does not currently properly check this."

